running-back-prospect-ak-dear-no-longer-team","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge questions LSU's claims the SEC 'hallucinated' citations","description":"At a hearing Wednesday in the SEC's lawsuit against LSU, a federal judge pushed back on LSU attorneys for using the word \"hallucinated\" in filing.","published":"2026-11-18T22:40:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522883/judge-questions-lsu-claims-sec-hallucinated-citations","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-18T22:17:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Urban Meyer not a candidate for open Maryland job","description":"Urban Meyer has not spoken to Maryland in any formal capacity about its vacant head coaching position and is not a candidate for the job, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-18T18:30:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522632/sources-urban-meyer-not-candidate-open-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Davenport RB Cephus Harris III to enter transfer portal","description":"Davenport's Cephus Harris III, the leading rusher in Division II and a candidate for the Harlon Hill Trophy, plans to enter the transfer portal, he told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-18T17:52:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522473/davenport-rb-cephus-harris-iii-enter-transfer-portal","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Top 25 betting lines: UGA big faves over Gamecocks, Vols slim favorites vs. LSU","description":"This week's odds and FPI predictions for South Carolina-Georgia, Tennessee-LSU and more.","published":"2026-11-18T14:36:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50498153/2026-college-football-week-12-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bottom 10 after Week 11: Paying tribute to our founding father","description":"The originator of celebrating football's downtrodden, former Los Angeles columnist Steve Harvey, died last week.","published":"2026-11-18T13:23:01.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50519786/bottom-10-week-11-clemson-steve-harvey","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McGee","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Take a 360-degree look at college football's iconic rivalry trophies","description":"Whether ancient, animal or absurd, college football's rivalry trophies take many shapes.","published":"2026-11-18T11:39:52.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/id/50371090/college-football-rivalry-trophies","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4921117/vicari-swain","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vicari_Swain"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Vicari Swain","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vicari_Swain","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:07Z","intro":"Vicari S. Swain (born September 12, 2004) is an American college football cornerback and return specialist for the South Carolina Gamecocks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Swain grew up in Carrollton, Georgia, and started playing football at age six. He attended Central High School where he competed in football and baseball and was a top defensive back and wide receiver in the former. As a junior, he posted 55 receptions for 855 yards and eight touchdowns along with 28 tackles and six interceptions. Swain then recorded 44 receptions for 610 yards and seven touchdowns along with 35 tackles and six interceptions as a senior in 2022. A four-star recruit, he committed to play college football for the South Carolina Gamecocks."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Swain appeared in three games for the Gamecocks as a true freshman in 2023. He then made 13 appearances as a backup cornerback in 2024, recording 13 tackles and a sack. He became a top cornerback and return specialist for the Gamecocks in 2025. In the first two games, Swain had three punt return touchdowns, earning Southeastern Conference (SEC) Special Teams Player of the Week both times. He returned a total of 19 punts for 302 yards and three touchdowns during the season, tying Kaden Wetjen for most punt return touchdowns nationally. He also posted 28 tackles, five pass breakups and two interceptions on defense."}]}}